{
  "id": "hutsul_music",
  "name": "Hutsulska muzyka (Hutsul Carpathian highland music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Music of the Hutsuls, Ukrainian highlanders of the eastern Carpathians around Verkhovyna, Kosiv and the Cheremosh valley. A band of fiddle, small tsymbaly dulcimer and drum (buben) plays kolomyiky and the hutsulka dance, while shepherding instruments, the long wooden trembita horn, sopilka and floiara flutes and the drymba jaw harp, serve signalling, funeral and pastoral music; kolomyika couplets and lyrical songs are sung in a strong, ornamented voice. The hammered-dulcimer card stands in for the tsymbaly and the frame-drum card for the buben.",
  "recipe": "classic modern hutsulska muzyka, field Work, Slavic balkan branch. fiddle, hammered dulcimer, credited frame drums, trembita, ornamented lively dance driving sopilka. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
